            <ArticleTitle>Acupuncture relief of chronic pain syndrome correlates with increased plasma met-enkephalin concentrations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1394-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In twenty patients with chronic pain syndrome, acupuncture treatment resulted in significant improvement of both pain and psychiatric symptoms and higher plasma concentrations of metenkephalin. Plasma beta-endorphin concentrations were unchanged. The degree of symptom relief was correlated with the increase in plasma met-enkephalin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
